---
// The client, the holder and the core. See reference/how-it-works.mdx.
---
<figure class="nerdr-diagram">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 760 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="dc-title dc-desc">
		<title id="dc-title">The client, the holder and the core</title>
		<desc id="dc-desc">
			The nerdr you start is a client. It connects to the core by the
			client socket. The holder starts the core, and starts and owns the
			agents, terminals and plugin runs. The holder and the core run on
			when the client is closed.
		</desc>
		<defs>
			<marker id="dc-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path class="arrowhead" d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" />
			</marker>
			<marker id="dc-arrow-accent" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
				<path class="arrowhead accent" d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		<!-- The client -->
		<rect class="box accent" x="10" y="176" width="140" height="70" rx="7" />
		<text class="title mono" x="80" y="205" text-anchor="middle">nerdr</text>
		<text class="sub" x="80" y="227" text-anchor="middle">the client</text>

		<!-- What runs on with no terminal -->
		<rect class="region dashed" x="262" y="12" width="486" height="276" rx="10" />
		<text class="region-label" x="280" y="38">Runs on when you close nerdr</text>

		<rect class="box" x="286" y="58" width="200" height="70" rx="7" />
		<text class="title" x="386" y="87" text-anchor="middle">holder</text>
		<text class="sub" x="386" y="109" text-anchor="middle">starts and owns the programs</text>

		<rect class="box" x="286" y="176" width="200" height="70" rx="7" />
		<text class="title" x="386" y="205" text-anchor="middle">core</text>
		<text class="sub" x="386" y="227" text-anchor="middle">the tabs and all the logic</text>

		<rect class="box" x="560" y="58" width="166" height="44" rx="7" />
		<text class="sub" x="643" y="85" text-anchor="middle">agents</text>
		<rect class="box" x="560" y="116" width="166" height="44" rx="7" />
		<text class="sub" x="643" y="143" text-anchor="middle">terminals</text>
		<rect class="box" x="560" y="174" width="166" height="44" rx="7" />
		<text class="sub" x="643" y="201" text-anchor="middle">plugin runs</text>

		<path class="edge" d="M486 80 H558" marker-end="url(#dc-arrow)" />
		<path class="edge" d="M486 93 C 520 93, 525 138, 558 138" marker-end="url(#dc-arrow)" />
		<path class="edge" d="M486 106 C 515 106, 525 196, 558 196" marker-end="url(#dc-arrow)" />

		<path class="edge" d="M386 128 V174" marker-end="url(#dc-arrow)" />
		<text class="edge-label" x="396" y="148">starts it,</text>
		<text class="edge-label" x="396" y="164">and again</text>

		<path class="edge accent" d="M150 211 H284" marker-start="url(#dc-arrow-accent)" marker-end="url(#dc-arrow-accent)" />
		<text class="edge-label accent" x="206" y="202" text-anchor="middle">client socket</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>
		Close nerdr and everything in the dashed box works on; start nerdr in
		the folder again to connect to it. If the core crashes, the holder
		starts it again. Quit stops it all.
	</figcaption>
</figure>
